          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: der Augenblick",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "der Augenblick — \"the moment, an instant\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Im letzten Augenblick sprang er in den Zug. At the last moment he jumped onto the train."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: die Augenblicke. Im Augenblick — at the moment, right now."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Augenblick comes from Middle High German ougenblick \"a quick glance\" (EtymDB), from Auge \"eye\" and Blick \"look\": the time an eye takes to blink."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
